WARNING:ENOSYS: ENOSYS means 'invalid syscall nr' and nothing else
#165: FILE: include/linux/kvm_host.h:864:
+	return -ENOSYS;

ENOSYS means that a nonexistent system call was called.
Earlier, it was wrongly used for things like invalid operations on
otherwise valid syscalls.  This should be avoided in new code.

See: https://lore.kernel.org/lkml/5eb299021dec23c1a48fa7d9f2c8b794e967766d.1408730669.git.luto@amacapital.net/

CHECK:UNNECESSARY_PARENTHESES: Unnecessary parentheses around 'eoifd->source != NULL'
#364: FILE: virt/kvm/eventfd.c:904:
+		if (eoifd->eventfd == eventfd &&
+		    eoifd->notifier.gsi == args->gsi &&
+		    uses_source == (eoifd->source != NULL)) {

Parentheses are not required in the following cases:

  1. Function pointer uses::

      (foo->bar)();

    could be::

      foo->bar();

  2. Comparisons in if::

      if ((foo->bar) && (foo->baz))
      if ((foo == bar))

    could be::

      if (foo->bar && foo->baz)
      if (foo == bar)

  3. addressof/dereference single Lvalues::

      &(foo->bar)
      *(foo->bar)

    could be::

      &foo->bar
      *foo->bar

